[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mollama_glm-5.1_cloud-integration-bug-trial-1[0m[0m
All 10 runs clean: no negative inventory, no ghost charges, no duplicate charges. Every run shows `Total charged == Expected charge`, stock never goes below zero, and duplicate charges is always 0.

**Summary of the fix (two files changed):**

**`inventory.py`** — Added `reserve()` method that atomically checks stock and decrements in one synchronous step (no `await` between the check and the mutation). This eliminates the TOCTOU race that caused overselling.

**`checkout.py`** — Replaced the three-phase `check_stock → charge → decrement` flow with a two-phase `reserve → charge` flow, with rollback via `increment` if charge fails. This eliminates ghost charges (customer charged but no item delivered) because stock is reserved before charging, and released back if the charge doesn't succeed.

The existing public methods (`check_stock`, `decrement`, `increment`, `charge`) are untouched; only a new `reserve()` method was added.
